These counts are sessions and assume independent sessions. Randomizing by visitor (as recommended) adds a design effect from repeat visits, so the real requirement is somewhat larger.{% set de = r.se_inflation_from_clustering ** 2 %} The variance inflation from clustering seen above (×{{ "%.2f" | format(de) }}) is a rough guide. A subtle change is not testable at current traffic. Test a bold change (25-50% target lift), use a higher-frequency primary metric (e.g. add-to-cart), or use CUPED with each visitor's pre-period activity to cut the sample needed. Randomizing by visitor also means the analysis must cluster by visitor, as above.
